new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e503e323
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-owner-signoff.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+### The train accepts an owner sign-off at a member's exact SHA (2026-11-08)
+
+When a branch reaches its review-round cap, the owner may approve one exact commit after Codex, Kimi
+and agy have all reviewed it (R-0618). `scripts/land/signoff.sh record` stores the approval as
+`refs/owner-signoff/<sha>`: the owner's verbatim words, the date, the SHA and the three reviewers'
+verdict outputs with their sha256. `train.sh`'s review provenance accepts, for a member with no clean
+review note, a sign-off that `signoff.sh verify` finds valid for that exact SHA, and then requires the
+train head to be exactly the clean merge of its members onto its base. A sign-off for another commit,
+a changed verdict file, a missing reviewer, a reviewer output ending in REJECT, a quote that names no
+commit, and a head beyond the clean merge are each refused (`scripts/checks/landing_script.sh`). The
+pre-push hook takes a sign-off push in its no-source-tree tier.
diff --git a/docs/LANDING.md b/docs/LANDING.md
index 63cfa3bf..87e62874 100644
--- a/docs/LANDING.md
+++ b/docs/LANDING.md
@@ -73,41 +73,46 @@ verdict; any failing leg fails the check (see [Pipelining](#pipelining)).
 - If `scripts/tests/select_gates.sh` (R-0513) exists and the hook does not already call it, its
   output is run as well. The interface is `select_gates.sh --base <sha> --head <sha>`, printing one
   gate command per line, which runs through `run_ci_gates_local.sh --first`.
 - **remote**: the full gate set (R-0541) through `LAND_REMOTE_RUNNER <ref> <command>`. The
   default runner is `~/bin/concrete-remote`; on the server it is `scripts/land/run-at-ref.sh`, which
   runs in a fresh `clone --local`, not a worktree, because some gates refuse linked worktrees. A
   runner that fetches from origin first gets the head published under a ref unique to that run,
   `wip/land-<name>-<sha>-<pid>-<n>` (the hook's backup tier). It is created only if absent. The
   push carries an empty lease, and ownership is taken only from `--porcelain`'s `*` (new ref)
   line, because git reports an existing ref at the same SHA as up to date before it checks the
   lease. On a collision the run tries a fresh name. The ref is deleted afterwards with a lease on
   that SHA, in one attempt that is never retried. A failed push may still have deleted it, so an
   unconfirmed deletion is reported and left alone. An EXIT backstop covers interruption before
   that attempt. As a result,
   concurrent checks never share or delete each other's refs. The run counts only if the runner reports
   `sha=<head>`. `--no-remote` skips this leg.
 - **review** (fails closed): the leg passes at once when the train already has **review
   provenance**: a clean review note at its head or, when the head has no note, a clean note on every
   member at its exact recorded SHA (each member was reviewed at its own head). Each note is judged by
   `scripts/review/verify.sh` on origin's notes; an absent, malformed, blocked or findings note
-  qualifies nothing, and a head note that is not clean is not overridden by the members. Otherwise
+  qualifies nothing, and a head note that is not clean is not overridden by the members. A member
+  without a clean note qualifies instead by an **owner sign-off** at its exact SHA (R-0618: a branch
+  at its review-round cap, approved by the owner after Codex, Kimi and agy all reviewed that commit;
+  `scripts/land/signoff.sh verify`, on origin's `refs/owner-signoff/*`). A sign-off approves that
+  commit only, so a train with a signed-off member must be exactly the clean merge of its members
+  onto its base: one conflict-free merge per member and nothing else. Otherwise
   the leg runs `LAND_REVIEW_CMD`, else `scripts/review/review.sh`, with `--base --head`, and then
   requires provenance: a non-zero exit fails, and so does a zero exit that leaves no clean note at the
 
  head. With no review command at all, `check` fails; it never disables the leg silently.
   `--no-review` skips the leg explicitly (the landing bot does, its members being reviewed), and
   `land` still requires review provenance. A review that refuses a patch recording an owner
   decision is answered in the review ([REVIEW.md](REVIEW.md#owner-decisions-choosing-versus-recording)),
   never by `--no-review`.
 - The per-leg durations, the wall time and their sum go to the log as a `check-legs` row.
 - Runs inside `nix develop` unless already in the dev shell. `LAND_NO_NIX=1` disables this.
 
 ### ci
 
 - Refuses unless `check` passed at this exact HEAD. Each `check` run first withdraws the previous
   pass, so a failed re-check leaves no pass behind. `--skip-check` overrides that, and the log
   records the check as `skipped`.
 - Pushes in two steps:
   1. `ci/<name>` is reset to the train's base. The base is main's own commit and has already been
      published, so this push skips the hook.
   2. The train is pushed on top with the hook running. The root hook builds the spec and runs
      the full root set; it reuses no record written by `check`. The push is verified (see [Verified pushes](#verified-pushes)).
diff --git a/docs/REVIEW.md b/docs/REVIEW.md
index 4f98a6cf..2a8fa9f4 100644
--- a/docs/REVIEW.md
+++ b/docs/REVIEW.md
@@ -159,38 +159,45 @@ A non-fast-forward rejection (another agent pushed notes in the meantime) is
 handled by fetching the remote notes, merging them (`git notes merge -s ours`: on
 a conflict for the same commit the local, newer note wins), and retrying, up to
 three attempts. Any other push failure stops at once with exit 6. The script also
 fetches and merges the remote notes before each round, so it counts rounds that
 were run elsewhere.
 
 The pre-push hook (`.githooks/pre-push`) runs no gates for a push that updates
 only these two notes refs: a notes commit holds one blob per annotated commit and
 no source tree. A push that also carries a branch takes that branch's tier.
 Until this hook reaches `main`, a hook installed from an older `main` still runs
 the gates on a note push, and the push fails outside `nix develop`.
 
 ## The cap
 
 At most `--max-rounds` rounds (default 5). When the last allowed round ends with
 findings or blocked pieces, the script records the note, prints the open
 findings, and exits 3. Asking for another round exits 3 without calling the
 reviewer. Do not work around the cap: split the branch into smaller branches or
 escalate to a human reviewer, and pass on the open findings.
 
+The owner may then approve one exact commit (R-0618), after Codex, Kimi and agy have all reviewed
+that commit. The approval is recorded, from the owner's own words only, with
+`scripts/land/signoff.sh record <sha> --date --quote --codex --kimi --agy` (each reviewer's verdict
+output, ending in `VERDICT: ACCEPT`) and pushed to both remotes as `refs/owner-signoff/<sha>`. The
+landing train accepts it as that commit's review provenance ([LANDING.md](LANDING.md)); it approves no
+other commit.
+
 ## verify.sh
 
 ```sh
 scripts/review/verify.sh <commit>          # exit 0 clean, 1 findings/blocked, 2 none or malformed
 scripts/review/verify.sh --fetch <commit>  # fetch the notes ref from origin first
 ```
 
 It judges the exact commit. A clean note on an ancestor says nothing about the
 commits after it, so a branch that gains a commit after its clean round needs
 another round.
 
 ## Tests
 
 `scripts/checks/review_tool.sh` runs the scripts against throwaway
 repositories, with a bare repository as `origin` and a fake `codex` that answers
 according to markers in the diff. It needs no API key. It covers delta selection,
 splitting, the refusal retry, the cap, note writing and pushing (including the
 non-fast-forward merge), verdict parsing, and `verify.sh`.


