     git hash-object [-t <type>] [-w] --stdin-paths [--no-filters]

DESCRIPTION
     Computes  the  object  ID value for an object with specified type with the
     contents of the named file (which can be outside of the  work  tree),  and
     optionally	 writes	 the resulting object into the object database. Reports
     its object ID to its standard output. When <type> is not specified, it de‐
     faults to "blob".

OPTIONS
     -t <type>
     --no-filters
	 Hash  the  contents  as  is, ignoring any input filter that would have
	 been chosen by the attributes	mechanism,  including  the  end-of-line
	 conversion.  If  the file is read from standard input then this is al‐
	 ways implied, unless the --path option is given.

     --literally
	 Allow --stdin to hash any garbage into a loose object which might  not
	 otherwise  pass standard object parsing or git-fsck checks. Useful for
	 stress-testing Git itself or reproducing characteristics of corrupt or
	 bogus objects encountered in the wild.

