• scripts/land/train.sh:518: The sign-off fallback never checks that the member reached its review-round cap. A member with no review history—or only a round-1 findings note—qualifies with three ACCEPT files and a sign-off, allowing a clean-merge train to land without the cap required by R-0618.

  scripts/land/signoff.sh:58: `git hash-object` applies configured clean filters and end-of-line conversion, while line 60 hashes the original file bytes. With CRLF verdict output and `core.autocrlf=true`, the stored blob contains LF but the recorded SHA-256 describes CRLF, so `record` creates a ref that its own verifier rejects. Use `git hash-object --no-filters`.

  .githooks/pre-push:49: The no-gates tier trusts only the destination ref name and never validates the pushed object as a sign-off record. `git push origin HEAD:refs/owner-signoff/arbitrary` publishes an ordinary source-commit tree without running any source gates; the new control likewise supplies an unrelated notes-commit SHA, so it cannot detect this case.

  VERDICT: REJECT

